9a73d393c30042","event_uuid":"e0c731d0-862f-4387-960b-33568679ca66","position":{"commit_sha":"3f2e302f64708474f3544f73c7d8d9ee31c0c746","position":"1786495892556343001-e0c731d0-862f-4387-960b-33568679ca66"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9301fce7c5df4284f4d29c41f3303fa97309919a680aa89c75211a9b3fe2fe47","event_uuid":"6b8bc41b-0a3d-406e-9099-d35f36d6c25c","position":{"commit_sha":"e1cfebf4bf1b4106f96a33f85e1c80ee1933ee6e","position":"1786497723870603888-6b8bc41b-0a3d-406e-9099-d35f36d6c25c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[],"created_at":1786486285728091001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1863e347-1f3c-403d-8f17-150f39be1d05","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"b902-18af-14ed-4da1"},{"link_uuid":"6b8bc41b-0a3d-406e-9099-d35f36d6c25c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2051-f4d8-8d29-4f55"}],"description":"## Context (measured 2026-08-11, analysis ticket b902-18af-14ed-4da1)\n\nZero of 2,093 recorded plan reviews carry a non-empty `overlap` block — the overlap feature (ADR 0086; ~13% of local usage-log LLM spend, ~$165/5 days plus its historical failure storms) has never surfaced a finding to a reviewer. An instrumented probe of `wire.overlap_findings` on 3 live tickets plus a controlled near-duplicate probe isolated a stacked root cause:\n\n1. **Batch-path verdicts systematically carry `confidence=0.0`.** Live `judge_batch` calls SUCCEED (no exception) and return entries with a real `relation` but `confidence=0.0` — including an unmistakable near-duplicate pair (same artifact, same feature, paraphrased titles), and every non-abstained real-pipeline verdict observed. `aggregate` requires BOTH orderings ≥ `overlap_conf_threshold` (0.7), so every pair dies. This has plausibly been fatal since batching landed (c403): the single-pair prompt/contract was calibrated for a confidence field the batched prompt path does not elicit.\n2. **Since 7fa8102477 (08-08), `output_token_limit=1024` truncates any real multi-candidate batch** (K up to 20 candidates → 10-pair batches; ~100+ tokens per verdict entry): the truncated response abstains the WHOLE batch. Probe: ordering-1 batches abstained for 31/31 candidates across 3 tickets. The fix for the 48k retry storms silently zeroed the surviving output path.\n\nUnit tests pass because they use canned runners; no live calibration case pins \"a near-duplicate pair actually surfaces\".\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Fix the batch contract so the model emits a meaningful `confidence` per entry (prompt-side: the overlap-judge prompt's confidence instructions must survive the batched rendering; verify with a live near-duplicate probe emitting confidence >= 0.7).\n2. Right-size the batch output budget: replace the flat `output_token_limit=1024` with a per-batch bound derived from the code's own batch cardinality constant (`_CANDIDATES_PER_CALL`) and a measured per-entry token allowance (measure a real verdict entry's token size in the calibration probe and add headroom), keeping `structured_retry_limit=0` and `transport_attempt_limit=1` so the 48k-storm class stays dead.\n3. Add a live calibration case (T5c discipline) asserting the near-duplicate pair surfaces and an unrelated pair does not, so this failure class cannot regress silently.\n4. Re-measure after landing: surfaced-findings rate over the next N reviews; if still ~0 with the mechanism healthy, THEN have the scrap-vs-keep conversation with working-feature data.\n\nOperator note: until this lands, the drain burns spend with provably zero output — pausing via the documented `overlap_drain = \"off\"` kill switch is reversible and recommended, but is the operator's call.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A live near-duplicate probe (two digests naming the same artifact and paraphrased scope) run through `judge_batch` in both orderings yields a non-abstain verdict with `confidence >= 0.7` in each ordering, and `aggregate` surfaces it. Verify: the new calibration script/test output committed with the change.\n- [ ] `judge_batch`'s output budget scales with the batch's pair count (no flat 1024), with `structured_retry_limit=0` and `transport_attempt_limit=1` retained. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_overlap_judge.py -x` passes including a new bound-scaling assertion.\n- [ ] An unrelated-pair probe still yields no surfaced finding (false-flag guard intact). Verify: same calibration evidence.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/overlap/judge.py","reason":"scale batch output budget; keep retry/transport bounds"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/reviewers/overlap_judge.md","reason":"batch-path confidence contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_overlap_judge.py","reason":"bound-scaling assertion + calibration pins"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2051-f4d8-8d29-4f55"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"9a408ee0-7a16-45c9-91c5-d2f1fc232d36","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"d147-c219-baf9-4e9e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Overlap detection has never surfaced a finding: batch-path verdicts carry confidence=0.0 and post-08-08 output cap truncates whole batches","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4622fa8d-673f-49a6-ac5a-248ac7421fa7","afd8c962-4499-4f10-9796-8b850c4acec8","34862a20-122d-4152-950e-d9589e8c3ee5","1863e347-1f3c-403d-8f17-150f39be1d05","40c729be-11ee-4f1a-99ac-e6720448f0a0","b604ff75-ec04-46ea-b606-a454b65aad2f","9a408ee0-7a16-45c9-91c5-d2f1fc232d36","e0c731d0-862f-4387-960b-33568679ca66","6b8bc41b-0a3d-406e-9099-d35f36d6c25c"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786497723870603889,"uuid":"389c6efc-be44-4e30-8dfc-dda50374d48f"}